nd ordinary amide cleavage. The sulfur-processing advantage and branching fraction are unknown.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_011", "rxn_012", "rxn_010"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_012", "mol_014", "mol_018", "mol_017"]}, {"pathway_id": "P4", "name": "Side-chain-first Strecker synthesis through thioamide and oxygen amide", "description": "Combine side-chain-first assembly with the candidate thioamide-to-oxygen-amide channel. This inherits both the early cyclization risk and the unmeasured sulfur-processing kinetics.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_011", "rxn_012", "rxn_010"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_016", "mol_014", "mol_018", "mol_017"]}, {"pathway_id": "P5", "name": "Ring-first Strecker synthesis through thioamide and thioacid", "description": "Test nitrogen-eliminating thioamide hydrolysis followed by thioacid hydrolysis. This is a competing mechanistic trace, not an independently demonstrated prebiotic synthesis route.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_011", "rxn_013", "rxn_014"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_012", "mol_014", "mol_018", "mol_019"]}, {"pathway_id": "P6", "name": "Side-chain-first Strecker synthesis through thioamide and thioacid", "description": "Combine side-chain-first aminonitrile construction with the candidate thioacid-processing channel. Productive flux through both conditional branches must be established independently.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_011", "rxn_013", "rxn_014"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_016", "mol_014", "mol_018", "mol_019"]}, {"pathway_id": "P7", "name": "Ring-first formate-Ugi synthesis", "description": "Use the heterocyclic imine, formic acid, and methyl isocyanide to install a protected amino-acid amide, then remove both protecting substituents hydrolytically. Isocyanide supply, ammonia-based coupling, and fin